eduka-customizer (0.13.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Users page: the live user with a password, without a password or with
    Debian's default, autologin and groups; accounts built into the image
    (create with or without a password, administrator, change or remove the
    password, delete). Also in the Quick Wizard, recipes ('users') and the
    command line ('eduka-customizer users').
  * Default time zone Asia/Dili (Timor-Leste) everywhere; choosing a
    language no longer changes the time zone.
  * The menu follows the order of the work, numbered from 1. Start to
    18. Build & Test, with Back and 'Next step' buttons on every page.
  * US English everywhere (boot menu 'Language' submenu, 'canceled').
  * Fixes from a code review (see CHANGELOG.md).

 -- Edukasaun OS Developers <dev@edukasaun.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000

eduka-customizer (0.12.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Language page: default language, keyboard (with variant), time zone,
    translations and spell checking for installed programs, a 'Language'
    submenu in the ISO boot menu and Calamares defaults. Also offered when a
    project is created from an ISO, a download or a new Debian base.
  * Calamares page: name, logo, icon and welcome images, colors, slideshow,
    desktop launcher, user and password rules, live user password,
    partitioning (file systems, swap, EFI size, encryption), requirements,
    restart, removed packages, and every configuration file.
  * Plymouth page: install themes from .deb, .zip, .tar.*, folders, .plymouth
    files or Debian packages; preview in a window; apply; remove; settings.
  * Boot Menu page: menu settings plus direct editing of grub.cfg,
    isolinux.cfg and the GRUB files inside the EFI image; edits are kept for
    every build; 'apply to the ISO now' rebuilds the ISO in seconds.
  * Kernel page: Debian, backports, Liquorix, XanMod, own repositories and
    .deb kernels; remove, hold, initramfs, ISO kernel, GRUB defaults of the
    installed system, firmware and DKMS.
  * Install applications with APT, Synaptic in a window or a terminal, also
    right before building.
  * Fixes: held packages counted as installed, append_params keeps unchanged
    lines, tzdata/locales installed when missing, Plymouth themes can be set
    where plymouth-set-default-theme is missing.

 -- Edukasaun OS Developers <dev@edukasaun.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

eduka-customizer (0.11.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Quick Wizard: build a complete distribution with Next, Next, Finish.
  * Distro Branding Studio: <id>-branding package replacing the identity of
    base-files, lsb-release, distro-info-data, desktop-base, Debian logos,
    GRUB (live and installed) and Calamares with dpkg diversions; optional
    <id>-archive-keyring with a generated signing key; editable Debian
    source trees.
  * Package Workshop: open installed packages, edit them directly, rebuild,
    install and hold; restore Debian's version.
  * Themes & Icons page, theme packs, theme import, desktop icons.
  * Login screens: LightDM GTK, Slick, Arctica, KDE greeters, SDDM themes,
    GDM, LXDM, Ly, greetd.
  * X11 / Wayland session choice and compositors (picom presets, built-in,
    labwc, KWin, Wayfire, Sway).
  * Live session: open the desktop's settings apps inside the session.
  * Developer logs and error reports in /tmp/eduka-customizer/.
  * Installable on Ubuntu and derivatives (PyQt6 or PyQt5, Python >= 3.9).

 -- Edukasaun OS Developers <dev@edukasaun.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0900

eduka-customizer (0.10.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Complete rewrite of Customizer as Eduka-Customizer for Edukasaun OS.
  * Python 3 and PyQt6; new GUI with sidebar navigation, live log and
    background tasks.
  * Debian stable, testing and sid only; Ubuntu and derivatives refused.
  * Debian live ISO support (live-boot), boot replay of the source ISO,
    generated hybrid BIOS/UEFI boot with optional Secure Boot.
  * Eduka-Desktop build/install and default settings, desktop environment
    and window manager switching, display managers and sessions.
  * Flatpak / Flathub support (install now or on first boot).
  * APT sources editor (deb822), packages, hooks, recipes, live edit
    session (Xephyr), Plymouth, wallpaper, login screen, QEMU testing.

 -- Edukasaun OS Developers <dev@edukasaun.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
